# Swift / iOS Conventions

## Architecture
- SwiftUI for UI. Observable ViewModels with `@Observable` macro (iOS 17+).
- Offline-first via PowerSync + Supabase. Local persistence during connectivity drops.
- Never inline hardware access in View code — import from `bridges/ios/`.

## AVFoundation (QR Scanning)
- QR scanning lives in `bridges/ios/QRScanner/`, exposed as a SwiftUI `UIViewControllerRepresentable`.
- Decode payload format: `gtr://part/{OEM}?batch={BATCH}` — pass decoded OEM part number to shared layer.
- No third-party HTML5/browser-based QR libraries.

## Biometric Auth
- Face ID / Touch ID via `bridges/ios/BiometricAuth/`.
- Used for staff POS/warehouse login alongside TOTP QR codes.

## GPS Tracking
- Location polling every ~5 seconds via `bridges/ios/LocationTracker/`.
- Push coordinates to Supabase Realtime for delivery tracking.

## Sync Rules
- Same conflict resolution as Android: server-wins for financial, last-write-wins for preferences.
- Never embed service_role keys — anon key + RLS only.

## Testing
- XCTest for ViewModels and business logic.
- UI tests for critical flows (search, add to cart, scan).
- Run `xcodebuild test -scheme GTRCustomer -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16'` before marking done.
